# netsurf: a sheet change that restyles a few elements re-cascades in place (patch 447)
# Generated 2026-11-25
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 446)
#
# "sheet change: an element's style changes" (the census's largest local
# decline: google, bbc, youtube) sent the batch to the full rebuild: 415's
# walk re-cascades the whole document with a fresh selection context and
# stopped at the first element whose style, ::before or ::after differs.
# For a sheet batch (it runs at the top, no mark state set; a removal or a
# root change runs inside a local change and keeps the decline) the walk
# now collects such elements -- at most 8, never the root -- and skips
# their subtrees. Every element outside them is compared with the fresh
# context, siblings included, so no sibling-selector check is needed. The
# context is installed and each element is restyled with its subtree
# through the class-change paths, as 370 answers a style attribute (its
# "old class" the current one: html_rl_sheet_hit_restyle). A restyle that
# declines leaves the batch to the full rebuild. More than 8: declined.
# Such a batch logs "LIFE SHEETINPLACE elements=N" and the sheet census lines
# a full rebuild of it would (316 SHEETCAUSE, 318 SHEETID, 321 SHEETREACH;
# macos9_sheet_census_lines, html_rl_take_inplace), so doc 23's census
# still sees every sheet batch that changes a style.
# Also: 446's sibling-parent decline names the parent's tag and box type.
#
